# REST API Example

> Credentials used for testing are stored in the `.env` file.
> Do not commit real credentials to GitHub.

## 1. Admin

### 1.1 Login

POST `http://localhost:9092/admin/login`

Content-Type: application/json

Credentials: `ADMIN_EMAIL`, `ADMIN_PASSWORD`

```json
{
    "email": "admin@example.com",
    "password": "your_password",
    "rememberMe": false
}
```

### 1.2 Register

POST `http://localhost:9092/admin/register`

Content-Type: application/json

```json
{
    "email": "admin@example.com",
    "password": "your_password"
}
```

### 1.3 Forgot Password

POST `http://localhost:9092/admin/forgot-password`

Content-Type: application/json

```json
{
    "email": "admin@example.com"
}
```

### 1.4 Profile

GET `http://localhost:9092/admin/profile`

Authorization: Bearer `YOUR_ADMIN_JWT`

## 2. User

### 2.1 Login

POST `http://localhost:9092/api/auth/local`

Content-Type: application/json

```json
{
    "identifier": "user@example.com",
    "password": "your_password"
}
```

### 2.2 Register

POST `http://localhost:9092/api/auth/local/register`

Content-Type: application/json

```json
{
    "username": "example_user",
    "email": "user@example.com",
    "password": "your_password"
}
```

### 2.3 Forgot Password

POST `http://localhost:9092/api/auth/forgot-password`

Content-Type: application/json

```json
{
    "email": "user@example.com"
}
```

### 2.4 Profile

GET `http://localhost:9092/api/users/me`

Authorization: Bearer `YOUR_USER_JWT`
